# Electronic stopping of a Si projectile in bulk Si, <001> channel, off-center 1/4
# trajectory, 12-valence-electron pseudopotential, after
#   T. Jarrin, Phys. Rev. B 112, 245202 (2025), Sec. III A and Figs. 2 and 4.
# Neutral Si projectile at 1 MeV (v = 1.19817 a.u.) moving along z at constant
# velocity (atoms_dyn IMPULSIVE: the target atoms stay fixed), with traveling
# pseudopotentials (traveling_pseudo ON).
#
# Differences with Jarrin (to keep the test small; this is a regression test,
# it does not reproduce his stopping power):
#   - 1x1x1 cubic cell (8 Si atoms, a = 5.431 A = 10.2631 bohr) instead of 3x3x3;
#   - pseudopotential: PseudoDojo ONCVPSP LDA scalar-relativistic, no core
#     correction, Si-sp (12 valence electrons: 2s 2p 3s 3p; Kleinman-Bylander
#     form), UPF format, downloaded from
#     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PseudoDojo/ONCVPSP-LDA-SR-noCCv0.4/master/Si/Si-sp.upf
#     instead of Jarrin's Hamann-type pseudopotential;
#   - 45 Ry cutoff instead of 220 Ry (PseudoDojo hints: 76 to 96 Ry);
#   - Gamma point only, Fermi smearing (8 empty bands) for a robust ground state;
#   - 20 time steps of 0.02 a.u. (the initial transient only).
#
# Geometry: in projection along z, the atomic columns are at (m, n) a/4 with
# m + n even; the channel centre (a/4, 0) has 4 columns at d = a/4. The
# off-center 1/4 position is at d/4 from the nearest column (0, 0):
# (x, y) = (a/16, 0). Start height z0 = 7a/16, where the projectile stays at
# least 3.66 bohr from all atoms along its path.
#
# 1) ground state of the 8 atoms + neutral projectile (projectile at rest)
set cell 10.2631 0 0 0 10.2631 0 0 0 10.2631 bohr
species silicon Si-sp.upf
species projectile Si-sp.upf
atom Si1 silicon 0.0000 0.0000 0.0000 bohr
atom Si2 silicon 0.0000 5.1315 5.1315 bohr
atom Si3 silicon 5.1315 0.0000 5.1315 bohr
atom Si4 silicon 5.1315 5.1315 0.0000 bohr
atom Si5 silicon 2.5658 2.5658 2.5658 bohr
atom Si6 silicon 2.5658 7.6973 7.6973 bohr
atom Si7 silicon 7.6973 2.5658 7.6973 bohr
atom Si8 silicon 7.6973 7.6973 2.5658 bohr
atom P projectile 0.6414 0.0000 4.4901 bohr 0.0 0.0 1.19817 atomicvelocity
set xc LDA
set ecut 45 rydberg
set ecutprec 6 rydberg
set force_complex_wf ON
set nempty 8
set smearing fermi
set smearing_width 0.01 hartree
set wf_dyn PSDA
set threshold_scf 1.E-8 5
randomize_wf
run 0 100 5

# 2) the projectile moves at constant velocity, traveling pseudopotentials
set atoms_dyn IMPULSIVE
set traveling_pseudo ON
set wf_dyn ETRS
set TD_dt 0.02 atomictime
set dt 0.02 atomictime
run 20 1
